    "narrative": "For the July 4th slate, the Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups, led by **Kyle Tucker** (71.26) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03). **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start despite the uncertainty of a pending lineup position; he benefits from a favorable matchup against the lefty Wandy Peralta, with the added benefit of recent form keeping his floor high. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** earns his high score through a perfect storm of an elite park environment and a favorable matchup against Sean Sullivan. **Andy Pages** (68.87) also projects as a strong play; his efficiency is bolstered by a high stolen base probability against a slow-working opponent, a key metric for our roster strategy given our emphasis on speed. **Gunnar Henderson** (63.22) rounds out our top-tier plays, as his ability to mitigate the skill of Greene provides the highest projected floor among our infielders.\n\nStrategic lineup construction forced a difficult decision at the corners, ultimately leaving **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.28) on the bench. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** possesses a high base projection, his efficiency for today is hampered by a significant negative park factor and a tough matchup against the talented Logan Gilbert, pushing him just below the threshold of our starters like **Josh Jung** and **Nolan Schanuel**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Jackson Merrill** (53.32); **Liam Hicks** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable matchup against Civale, while **Jackson Merrill** faces an uphill climb against the elite arsenal of Yoshinobu Yamamoto, making his lower efficiency score a potential risk point. Weather and late-scratches for the pending lineups remain our primary tactical concerns, but we are well-positioned to maintain our category leads as long as our speed-heavy outfielders capitalize on their projected base-stealing opportunities.",
